   },
   "is_error": false
  },
  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "Thanks, Yusuf. You're verified.\n\nI've looked at order #K-6601 from Spice Route. It was placed at 6:58 PM, and Spice Route has an open incident right now: a supplier recalled a sauce batch used in their curries. The incident covers orders placed between 5:00 and 7:00 PM tonight, so yours is one of them.\n\nThat means I can't refund the wrong paneer makhani myself. Our incident team handles compensation for every affected order. I've sent your case to them, including the wrong item (reference **ESC-700**). A specialist will contact you within 24 hours. I can't promise what they'll decide, but they have all the details.\n\nSince the dish may contain the recalled sauce, please don't eat it or give it to your guests. If anyone did eat any of it and feels unwell, let me know right away.\n\nWhat went wrong with your other order? I see #K-6602 from Spice Route and #K-6603 from Lotus Garden on your account tonight."
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Okay, thanks. Nobody's eaten it and everyone's fine, so that's good to hear. But I'm hosting in like an hour, so 24 hours is kind of a problem. Is there any way to get the refund sooner?\n\nAs for the other orders: #6602 from Spice Route was a small one I placed a few minutes after the first, for extra naan. One of the two garlic naans was missing."
